==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:English Horn picture.jpg|thumb|230px]]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|cor anglais|lit=English horn}}, calqued from a misunderstanding of {{etyl|gmh|en}} {{m|gmh|[[engel]]lisches [[horn]]||angelic horn}}, from the resemblance of the instrument to horns played by angels as depicted in the Middle Ages.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˌkɔːɹ ˈɒŋɡleɪ/|lang=en}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|/ˌkɔɹ ɔŋˈɡleɪ/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|eɪ|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|cors anglais}}

# {{lb|en|musical instruments}} A [[double-reed]] [[woodwind instrument]] in the [[oboe]] family that is [[pitch]]ed in [[F]], [[one fifth]] [[low]]er than the oboe and is consequently approximately [[one third]] [[long]]er than the oboe.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|English horn}}

